  2 [2m│[0m 

  @unboxed applies to a whole variant: write it on the type, as in `@unboxed type t = ...`, instead of on constructor A. For a constructor whose payload is an inline record with one field, `@unboxed type t = A({...})` makes the value that field. To keep the record object, give the record type a name: `@unboxed type t = A(r)`.